1
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,079
Xiao Qi

2
00:00:43,479 --> 00:00:44,399
Let go of me!

3
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,159
What are you doing? Let go of me!

4
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,200
Go tell Wang Xiang

5
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:48,920
Let go!

6
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:50,439
Trade the shop for her

7
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,200
Let go!

8
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:01,079
Uncle Xiang

9
00:01:02,159 --> 00:01:02,840
Something's wrong!

10
00:01:03,159 --> 00:01:04,319
Danni's being held at the nightclub!

11
00:01:06,159 --> 00:01:06,680
Maybe we should...

12
00:01:06,799 --> 00:01:07,280
Call the police

13
00:01:07,280 --> 00:01:07,760
Don't call yet

14
00:01:09,959 --> 00:01:11,200
What they want is the flower shop

15
00:01:11,599 --> 00:01:12,840
Danni should be safe

16
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:14,400
I'll go bring her back

17
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,280
You wait for me here

18
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,040
Liang Zhiqiang.

19
00:01:30,599 --> 00:01:31,079
Boss.

20
00:01:31,359 --> 00:01:32,319
The reason we never got that shop

21
00:01:32,319 --> 00:01:33,319
was because of this guy.

22
00:01:37,159 --> 00:01:39,239
He stopped us from taking it last time,

23
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,159
and now he's on my turf.

24
00:01:41,159 --> 00:01:42,200
Who the hell are you?

25
00:01:43,159 --> 00:01:43,959
Let her go.

26
00:01:44,879 --> 00:01:46,640
Can't even introduce yourself,

27
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,400
yet you barge onto my turf barking orders?

28
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:53,200
This woman hit one of my brothers,

29
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,599
and she thinks she's in the right?

30
00:01:55,799 --> 00:01:56,599
That's right.

31
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:58,319
Half my face is still swollen.

32
00:01:58,480 --> 00:01:59,439
It hurts so bad.

33
00:02:00,599 --> 00:02:01,599
How do you want to settle this?

34
00:02:02,879 --> 00:02:05,599
Settle it? Do you even have a say?

35
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,640
Let's hear it.

36
00:02:07,799 --> 00:02:09,560
About that shop business,

37
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:10,960
we've been at it several times now.

38
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:12,960
Dragging it out like this,

39
00:02:13,439 --> 00:02:14,759
it's driving me crazy.

40
00:02:15,639 --> 00:02:16,159
Here's the deal.

41
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:17,639
Hand over the deed,

42
00:02:17,639 --> 00:02:18,159
and you can take her.

43
00:02:18,159 --> 00:02:18,960
In your dreams.

44
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,280
Let her go.

45
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:23,879
Whatever your problem is, take it up with me.

46
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:25,439
Take it up with you?

47
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:36,000
Oh, I love this kind of scene.

48
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Hero saves the damsel.

49
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,479
So heroic.

50
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:40,599
Do me a favor.

51
00:02:40,879 --> 00:02:41,759
A favor?

52
00:02:42,879 --> 00:02:44,080
Who do you think you are?

53
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,520
Why should I do you any favors?

54
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,960
This place belongs to the United Righteous Group.

55
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,680
Xie Guanhong is my brother.

56
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,759
Consider it a favor to him.

57
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,840
So you're Brother Hong's man?

58
00:02:59,159 --> 00:03:01,639
Of course I'll give Brother Hong that respect.

59
00:03:01,639 --> 00:03:02,719
Come on, come on.

60
00:03:02,719 --> 00:03:04,360
Out at this hour, you haven't eaten yet, right?

61
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,000
Come, come.

62
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:05,639
Let's talk over some food.

63
00:03:05,639 --> 00:03:06,439
Talk over some food.

64
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:10,599
Why aren't you eating?

65
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,680
Can't handle spicy, huh?

66
00:03:14,759 --> 00:03:16,199
How many times have I told you,

67
00:03:16,199 --> 00:03:18,719
prep a half-and-half hot pot when guests come.

68
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,240
No utensils, is that it?

69
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:29,639
Chopsticks, get the chopsticks.

70
00:03:32,400 --> 00:03:33,319
Sorry about that.

71
00:03:33,599 --> 00:03:34,879
We don't have any spare chopsticks.

72
00:03:35,319 --> 00:03:36,199
So how about this,

73
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,280
just make do and eat.

74
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:43,599
Eat.

75
00:04:13,759 --> 00:04:14,639
Enough, Elephant.

76
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,399
Don't throw your weight around here.

77
00:04:17,279 --> 00:04:19,000
Fine, fine, fine.

78
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,040
You know me...

79
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:22,639
I just love people with backbone like you.

80
00:04:23,839 --> 00:04:25,040
This whole thing...

81
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,639
It's really not that big a deal.

82
00:04:27,279 --> 00:04:28,079
Tell you what.

83
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:31,120
Drink down this pot of soup,

84
00:04:31,639 --> 00:04:34,639
then kneel and kowtow to me three times,

85
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:36,680
and I'll let her go.

86
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:39,759
How about it? Generous enough for you?

87
00:04:40,839 --> 00:04:42,279
Liang Zhiqiang, don't listen to him!

88
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,360
Or how about this instead?

89
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:52,399
Me, I love a fiery girl the most.

90
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:55,240
I'll have my fun with her for a few days,

91
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:58,360
and once I'm done, I'll give her back.

92
00:04:58,959 --> 00:05:00,319
As for the shop...

93
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,959
we'll call it even.

94
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:02,920
So, what'll it be?

95
00:05:14,240 --> 00:05:16,279
What the hell is wrong with you?

96
00:06:00,439 --> 00:06:01,120
Let's go!

97
00:06:06,319 --> 00:06:07,000
Hurry!

98
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:12,399
Let me do it

99
00:07:28,079 --> 00:07:29,759
You really don't seem like a modern guy

100
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:33,480
Even your place looks like an antique

101
00:07:34,079 --> 00:07:34,759
Yeah

102
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:38,519
Some things are just better old

103
00:07:49,759 --> 00:07:50,800
Just make do.

104
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,480
Is this all you have at home?

105
00:07:53,439 --> 00:07:54,839
It's already quite a feast.

106
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:03,319
That's not for eating.

107
00:08:04,959 --> 00:08:06,199
What are you thinking?

108
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,800
I just wanted a look.

109
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:08,800
It's pretty cute.

110
00:08:13,639 --> 00:08:15,120
It was like this when I was little too.

111
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:16,920
I'd wake up hungry at night,

112
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:19,480
and sneak off to boil noodles with an egg.

113
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:20,920
Really?

114
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:24,240
You never told me about your childhood.

115
00:08:26,399 --> 00:08:27,839
We were really poor back then.

116
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:30,839
Luckily we lived by the sea, so we had fish.

117
00:08:31,399 --> 00:08:32,320
We never went hungry.

118
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,519
I still remember, back then with Ah Hong,

119
00:08:36,519 --> 00:08:37,720
we loved going to the pier the most.

120
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:39,320
Watching the sea, playing around.

121
00:08:39,799 --> 00:08:42,919
And the fishermen coming back with their catch,

122
00:08:43,399 --> 00:08:45,159
they'd call us over to haul the fish.

123
00:08:46,080 --> 00:08:47,000
It stank so bad!

124
00:08:49,279 --> 00:08:50,120
So what happened after that?

125
00:08:50,559 --> 00:08:52,159
How did you end up in Harbor City?

126
00:08:57,519 --> 00:08:58,480
Later on...

127
00:08:59,399 --> 00:09:00,480
the boat capsized.

128
00:09:02,399 --> 00:09:03,519
Both our families were gone.

129
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,840
Ah Hong and I couldn't stay in school.

130
00:09:07,559 --> 00:09:08,840
We had no other choice.

131
00:09:09,279 --> 00:09:11,639
We took a boat out to make a living.

132
00:09:13,679 --> 00:09:15,159
When we first came to Harbor City,

133
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:18,039
no one would even hire us to wash dishes.

134
00:09:20,279 --> 00:09:21,879
We didn't have a single cent on us.

135
00:09:21,960 --> 00:09:24,720
We had to scavenge leftover boxed meals off the street.

136
00:09:24,879 --> 00:09:25,919
We shared them.

137
00:09:33,120 --> 00:09:34,240
So then...

138
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:38,440
how'd you become a young gangster?

139
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:44,279
We had no choice.

140
00:09:46,039 --> 00:09:47,360
Either be a young gangster,

141
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:48,519
or...

142
00:09:49,559 --> 00:09:50,639
starve to death in the streets.

143
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:02,039
Ah Hong and I were like real brothers.

144
00:10:03,559 --> 00:10:05,080
We always have been.

145
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,039
After I got out, I felt like...

146
00:10:12,559 --> 00:10:14,200
this world had changed so much.

147
00:10:15,159 --> 00:10:16,360
People had changed a lot too.

148
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:18,360
All these cell phones,

149
00:10:18,399 --> 00:10:19,440
these towering buildings.

150
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,200
I didn't even know what they were.

151
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,279
And no one to ask, either.

152
00:10:23,519 --> 00:10:24,399
Ah Hong was the same.

153
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,759
He seemed like he hadn't changed,

154
00:10:27,559 --> 00:10:30,320
but really, he'd changed so much.

155
00:10:35,679 --> 00:10:37,399
Then I want to ask you something.

156
00:10:40,279 --> 00:10:42,320
How come you never seemed afraid of me?

157
00:10:42,399 --> 00:10:44,000
Even knowing I did 20 years inside.

158
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,200
To tell the truth,

159
00:10:50,799 --> 00:10:52,039
I was scared at first.

160
00:10:53,559 --> 00:10:54,879
I was afraid you were a gangster.

161
00:10:56,559 --> 00:10:57,639
I hate gangsters.

162
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,879
I don't want anything to do with them.

163
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,039
But...

164
00:11:06,519 --> 00:11:07,600
when I looked at you,

165
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,919
always alone,

166
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,200
always so quiet,

167
00:11:10,519 --> 00:11:12,039
always with your head down,

168
00:11:14,879 --> 00:11:15,879
sometimes...

169
00:11:16,919 --> 00:11:19,320
looking so pitiful in a corner,

170
00:11:19,519 --> 00:11:20,600
just like...

171
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:26,120
like a drowned puppy.

172
00:11:29,559 --> 00:11:30,480
That's when I knew

173
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,720
you weren't like them.

174
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,919
Today, we're both drowned puppies.

175
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,320
That's not true.

176
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,480
What I saw today

177
00:11:42,799 --> 00:11:43,720
is a wolf.
